# Bulk: raw corpora, substrate artifacts, per-run outputs, scratch.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is the whole point of this comment. Unanchored, `data/`
# matches at ANY depth — including `src/mtlcheck/data/`, which silently left the entire layer-2
# package unversioned for the life of the project. Three commits claimed changes to files inside it
# and contained none of them. Never unanchor these.
/data/
/artifacts/
/runs/
/scratch/

# Re-include the source package that the bulk patterns were swallowing. `src/mtlcheck/data/` is the
# layer-2 code, not a data directory, and it went unversioned for the life of the project because an
# unanchored `data` pattern — here AND in the shared .git/info/exclude, which this file outranks —
# matched it at depth. Three commits claimed changes to files inside it and carried none.
!/src/mtlcheck/data/
!/src/mtlcheck/data/**

# ...with one deliberate exception. A substrate is 44 GB and cannot live in git, but the CLAIM that
# a given substrate exists — its build config, content hashes, edge counts, row-space provenance —
# is the scientific record, and the E10 equivalence test validates against exactly these numbers.
!artifacts/
artifacts/*
!artifacts/substrate/
artifacts/substrate/*
!artifacts/substrate/*/
artifacts/substrate/*/*
!artifacts/substrate/*/*/
artifacts/substrate/*/*/*
!artifacts/substrate/*/*/manifest.json

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store
.pending/
